{"BawaH": [{"id": "BawaH", "headword": "भटः", "headword_slp1": "BawaH", "fold": "BawaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "भटः [bhaṭḥ], [भट्-अच्]", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A warrior, soldier, combatant; दीन परिजनकृताश्रुजलो न भटीजनः स्थिरमना विचक्लमे Śi.15.93; तद्भटचातुरीतुरी N.1.12; वादित्रसृष्टिर्घटते भटस्य 22.22; Bk. 14.11.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A mercenary, hired soldier, hireling.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "An outcast, a barbarian.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A demon.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of a degraded tribe.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A servant, slave. -टा Coloquintida (इंद्रवारुणी). -Comp. -पेटकम् a troop of soldiers. -बलाग्रः a hero; Buddh. (-ग्रम्) an army.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["bhaTa", "bhaTaH", "bhaṭa", "bhaṭaḥ", "भट"], "synonyms_slp1": ["bhaTa", "bhaTaH", "bhaṭa", "bhaṭaḥ", "Bawa"]}, {"id": "BawwaH", "headword": "भट्टः", "headword_slp1": "BawwaH", "fold": "BawaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "भट्टः [bhaṭṭḥ], [भट्-तन्]", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A lord, master (used as a title of respect in addressing princes).", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A title used with the names of learned Brāhmaṇas; भट्टगोपालस्य पौत्रः Māl.1; so कुमारिलभट्टः &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Any learned man or philosopher.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A kind of mixed caste, whose occupation is that of bards or panegyrists; क्षत्रियाद्विप्रकन्यायां भट्टो जातो$नुवाचकः । वैश्यायां शूद्रवीर्येण पुमानेको बभूव ह । स भट्टो वाव- दूकश्च सर्वेषां स्तुतिपाठकः ॥ Brav. P.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A bard, panegyrist.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Comp. आचार्यः a title given to a learned man or any celebrated teacher (esp. कुमारिलभट्ट).", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a great doctor. -नारायणः N. of the author of वेणीसंहारम्. -प्रयागः = प्रयाग q. v.", "gloss_lan